From: Shimazu <vanessimbolon2020@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 02:19:04 +0000
Subject: GEditorContent: Replace legacy ItemStack data-value constructor with named stained glass materials

AE PATCH REASON: Legacy ItemStack(Material, int, short) damage-value constructor is deprecated and removed on modern Bukkit/Paper versions after the 1.13 flattening; it fails to compile against current Paper API.
AE PATCH FIX: Replace new ItemStack(Material.GLASS, 1, (short)15/5/14) with named stained-glass materials BLACK_STAINED_GLASS, LIME_STAINED_GLASS and RED_STAINED_GLASS, preserving the original glass colors.
AE PATCH RISK: LOW - API: legacy ItemStack damage-value constructor → named materials. No behavior change.

---
diff --git a/net/advancedplugins/ae/features/gkits/editor/GEditorContent.java b/net/advancedplugins/ae/features/gkits/editor/GEditorContent.java
--- a/net/advancedplugins/ae/features/gkits/editor/GEditorContent.java	2026-07-30 10:27:31.681350240 +0000
+++ b/net/advancedplugins/ae/features/gkits/editor/GEditorContent.java	2026-07-31 00:31:12.024389898 +0000
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@
 
    public void openInventory() {
       Inventory var1 = Bukkit.createInventory(null, 36, "§eGContent:§6 " + this.kit);
-      ItemStack var2 = new ItemStack(Material.GLASS, 1, (short)15);
+      ItemStack var2 = new ItemStack(Material.BLACK_STAINED_GLASS);
       ItemMeta var3 = var2.getItemMeta();
       var3.setDisplayName(" ");
       var2.setItemMeta(var3);
@@ -30,11 +30,11 @@
          var1.setItem(var5, var2);
       }
 
-      ItemStack var10 = new ItemStack(Material.GLASS, 1, (short)5);
+      ItemStack var10 = new ItemStack(Material.LIME_STAINED_GLASS);
       ItemMeta var11 = var10.getItemMeta();
       var11.setDisplayName("§aSave Kit");
       var10.setItemMeta(var11);
-      ItemStack var6 = new ItemStack(Material.GLASS, 1, (short)14);
+      ItemStack var6 = new ItemStack(Material.RED_STAINED_GLASS);
       ItemMeta var7 = var6.getItemMeta();
       var7.setDisplayName("§cCancel Progress");
       var6.setItemMeta(var7);
